# BackitSnappy doesn't read a .env file -- this documents what you'll need,
# it isn't consumed by the app. All of these are entered through the app's
# own setup screen on first launch and stored in the macOS Keychain, never
# on disk in plaintext. Copy this file's *values* into the setup screen when
# prompted, not into an actual .env.

# From https://my.telegram.org/apps (log in with your phone number, create
# an app if you don't have one yet).
TELEGRAM_API_ID=1234567
TELEGRAM_API_HASH=0123456789abcdef0123456789abcdef

# Everything below is generated automatically by the app -- nothing to fill
# in yourself, listed here only so the full picture of what's stored is
# clear:
#   - Telegram session string (created after you sign in)
#   - iOS Shortcut pairing token (rotatable from Settings)
#   - "BackitSnappy Storage" channel ID (created on first sign-in)
#   - "iPhone Backup" album ID (created on first sign-in)
